window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Finnick O'Reilly became my dark prince the day he rescued me from my bullies. </b>I hoped and prayed that my savior would return after the day he saved me, but he never did. I was heartbroken, but it was for the best.<br> He saved me just to torment everyone else in Grove Hill.<br> People shiver at his name. He is one of the Bastards of Grove Hill. He's a thug, a criminal, and I'm so glad I've managed to not attract his attention since the day he saved me.<br> That is until the day he sees me.<br> Now, he wants me and he'll stop at nothing to make me his. I'm the only person who doesn't cower at his name. He doesn't scare me and that's something he admires.<br> Finnick is possessive, controlling, manipulative, and he's one man you don't want to fight with yet I do.<br> Still, I fall into his trap. Now, I'm stuck in a bet with him I shouldn't have ever made. The bet is simple. He wants my virginity. I refuse to be bedded by a man I'm not in love with. He has six weeks to get me to fall in love with him or he has to leave me alone forever.<br> I'm not sure anymore which one of those options is worse.<br> ~<br> <i>Reckless is the first book in the Bastards of Grove Hill series. It is necessary to listen to the books in order. A series order is available on the author's website along with a full list of content warnings.</i></p>"; 
